What:		/sys/devices/platform/10006000.power-controller/*suspend/state
Date:		October 2026
Contact:	FuQuan <i@fuquan.moe>
Description:
		Read-only diagnostic snapshot of the MT6580 PCM suspend provider.
		mode=load-only identifies the initial instruction-fetch stage;
		mode=retained-run executes PCM with retention flags and clock/memory
		requests held. R7 is connected for timer/control sequencing; R0
		crystal control remains disconnected.
		pcm_words and dma identify the coherent instruction buffer. loads
		counts completed instruction fetches, not PCM sleep executions.
		last_error is the last loader/handoff errno; loaded_fsm and
		restored_fsm record its hardware FSM values. fsm/con0/con1/pwr_io
		are live always-on SPM registers. No write operation is provided.
		runs counts execution attempts, irqs counts normal IRQ handler
		dispatches, and pending records the GIC pending state at cleanup.
		Normal suspend return is acknowledged in the atomic entry callback,
		so irqs may remain zero despite a real SPM timer wake. forced_exit
		means CPU_WAKE was requested after an external IRQ returned WFI.
		wake fields contain PCM R11/R12/R13, raw/misc/timer, return ISR,
		event, PC, assertion and debug snapshots. power/power2 compare the
		two power-status registers before and after the retained run.
		timer_cfg/val/at_wake record timer setup and its state immediately
		after WFI, before any forced PCM exit. wake_pwr_io/flags/src_req
		record the applied R7 connection and retention constraints.
		source before/applied record the original and selected SRC_REQ;
		CCIF event masks are preserved, APSRC bit 0 stays asserted, and
		software F26M bit 1 is omitted only if all configured UARTs completed
		their sleep handshake and DISP/MFG are off. blockers bits retain
		F26M for an unready UART (0), powered DISP/MFG (1), an unqualified
		POWER_ON_VAL0/1 baseline (2), or an existing firmware F26M request
		(3). Source snapshots also include pre-run R13, POWER_ON_VAL0/1,
		CLK_CON, AP_STANDBY and MMDDR_MASK. These show request ownership;
		they do not establish that 26 MHz physically stopped. R0 output
		remains disconnected and APSRC retained in either policy.
		cpu0 mode/resumes/result record CPU0 resume-entry qualification.
		vector contains the original/programmed/restored shared boot
		address; timer_ctrl and counter contain before/after physical
		timer snapshots. resumes counts returns through cpu_resume.

What:		/sys/devices/platform/10006000.power-controller/*suspend/cpu0_mode
Date:		October 2026
Contact:	FuQuan <i@fuquan.moe>
Description:
		CPU0 entry mode for explicit standby: 0 (default) retains normal
		WFI, 1 saves ARM/CPU-PM context, waits for wakeup, then performs
		a software MMU-off restart through cpu_resume before restoring
		the original shared boot vector and PM state. Mode 1 keeps CPU0,
		L2, infra, DDR and supplies powered; it qualifies the resume entry
		and does not prove hardware power-down or Boot ROM handoff.
		Android's default s2idle is unchanged. Values above 1 are rejected.

What:		/sys/devices/platform/10006000.power-controller/*suspend/pcm_timer_ms
Date:		October 2026
Contact:	FuQuan <i@fuquan.moe>
Description:
		Optional PCM timer for explicit standby, in milliseconds, 0..60000.
		Default 0 disables it and uses external wakeup. A nonzero value
		arms a 32.768 kHz PCM timer for the next standby entry. It neither
		changes Android's default s2idle policy nor enables power gating.

What:		/sys/devices/platform/1000f000.pmic-wrap/spm_phase
Date:		October 2026
Contact:	FuQuan <i@fuquan.moe>
Description:
		Read-only snapshot of the MT6350 suspend command-slot handoff.
		active indicates an installed suspend table. prepared counts
		successful installations; restored counts successful restores,
		including rollback. saved and staged retain the latest four
		words in ADR4/WDATA4/ADR5/WDATA5 order. They are snapshots, not
		live reads. Staging slots does not execute a PMIC command or
		change voltage; no write operation is provided.
		auxadc contains STRUP_CON10 saved/resume/restored snapshots. After
		PCM execution, only its START bit is restored before releasing the
		slots; unrelated PMIC bits are retained.
